From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PonWrt Maintainers <ponwrt@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93: enforce the 32-bit DMA address limit

EIP93 descriptor and ring address registers are 32-bit wide. Set both the
streaming and coherent DMA masks before allocating rings or mapping request
buffers, rather than relying on the platform's implicit default mask.

---
--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
@@ -422,2 +422,5 @@ static int eip93_crypto_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	eip93->dev = dev;
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, eip93);
